               <head>Shabistān-i nikāt va gulistān-i lughāt by Fattāḥī Nīshābūri</head>
               <msContents
                  class="http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008104964 http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85100076 
                  http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85003642">
                  <summary>A Persian allegorical treatise, also known as <title>Shabistān-i
                        khayāl</title>, composed in mixed prose and verse on morality from Sufi
                     perspective. </summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="Uk_Delhi_Persian_929-item1">
                     <author key="VIAF_71533966">
                        <persName xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc">Fattāḥī, Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Sībak
                           (d.852/1448-9)i</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="fa">فتاحی، محمد یحیى ابن سیبک</persName>
                     </author>
                     <title xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" key="work_7200">Shabistān-i nikāt va gulistān-i
                        lughāt</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa" key="work_7200">شبستان نکات و گلستان لغات</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" type="alt" key="work_7200">Shabistān-i
                        khayāl</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa" type="alt" key="work_7200">شبستان خیال</title>
                     <incipit xml:lang="fa">حمد خدای را که چشمه میم حمدش دریاییست</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="fa">شب ظلمت از روی او دور دار - ستان آنگهش از قبول
                        نظر</explicit>
                     <colophon>(f. 70v) Completed in 1096 (December 1684-November 1685) by <persName
                           role="scr">Muḥammad Balkhī Khāksār</persName>. </colophon>
                     <note>Title is abbreviated to <title>Shabistān-i nikāt</title> in note on f.1r
                        and cover label. </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="fa">Persian</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <physDesc>
                  <objectDesc form="codex">
                     <supportDesc material="chart">
                        <extent>ff. 71. <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                              <height>180</height>
                              <width>108</width>
                           </dimensions>
                           <dimensions type="written" unit="mm">
                              <height>125</height>
                              <width>58</width>
                           </dimensions>
                        </extent>
                        <foliation>
                           <p>Stamped foliation throughout; pencilled foliation every five leaves.
                           </p>
                        </foliation>
                        <collation>
                           <p>
                              <catchwords>Catchwords on the bottom left of the verso. </catchwords>
                           </p>
                        </collation>
                        <condition>
                           <p>Worm-eaten and damaged. Detached from binding with most stitchings
                              broken. The cover is also worm-eaten and damaged. </p>
                        </condition>
                     </supportDesc>
                     <layoutDesc>
                        <layout columns="1" ruledLines="15">
                           <p>15 lines per page. </p>
                        </layout>
                     </layoutDesc>
                  </objectDesc>
                  <handDesc>
                     <summary/>
                     <handNote>
                        <p>Fine nastaʻlīq; copied in black ink, with headings and markings in red.
                           Copyist: <persName role="scr" key="person_f9043">Muḥammad Balkhī Khāksār. </persName>
                        </p>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  <decoDesc>
                     <p/>
                  </decoDesc>
                  <additions>
                     <p>Note on f. 1r mentioning the title of the work and stating that it had been
                        bought in '<hi rend="italic">dār al-khilāfah</hi>' (perhaps Delhi). </p>
                     <p>Marginal and interlinear notes throughout the first eight folios, giving
                        interpretations and explanations, often rhetorical and not mystical/moral. </p>
                     <p>Folio 71v contains a few lines of poetry by the poet <persName role="aut"
                           key="person_91000370">Ṣāʾib Tabrīzī</persName>. </p>
                  </additions>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <binding notBefore="1800" notAfter="1857">
                        <decoNote>Brown leather contemporaneous Indian binding with central
                           partially preserved paper medallion, vertical pendants (one above and one
                           below), corners, and double ruled gilt-painted frame. </decoNote>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
                  <sealDesc>
                     <seal subtype="rectangle" type="stamp">
                        <p>Rectangular seal of former owner <persName role="fmo" key="person_f8599">Sayyid Saʿīd
                              ʿAlī Khān</persName>, dated 1167 (1753-54) (f. 1r). </p>
                     </seal>
                     <seal subtype="oval" type="stamp">
                        <p>Black Government of India Delhi MSS oval stamp (ff. 1r, 70v). </p>
                     </seal>
                  </sealDesc>
               </physDesc>
               <history>
                  <origin><origDate calendar="Hijri-qamari" notBefore="1684-12-07"
                        notAfter="1685-11-28">AH 1096 (December 1684-November 1685)</origDate>
                     <origPlace>probably in India</origPlace>/> </origin>
                  <provenance>
                     <p>Belonged to <persName role="fmo" key="person_f8599">Sayyid Saʿīd ʿAlī Khān</persName> in the second half of the 18th century (his seal dated
                        1167/1753-4) who also owned <ref
                           target="https://www.fihrist.org.uk/catalog/manuscript_17788">Delhi
                           Persian 72</ref> and <ref
                           target="https://www.fihrist.org.uk/catalog/manuscript_32797">Delhi
                           Persian 911A. </ref></p>
                     <p>Part of the Delhi collection of manuscripts which was purchased by the
                        Government of India at a sale organised by Delhi Prize Agents in
                           <date>1859</date>. </p>
                  </provenance>
                  <acquisition>
                     <p>Acquired by the India Office Library as an administrative deposit in
                           <date>1876</date>. </p>
                  </acquisition>
               </history>
